Looking at your template, I can see two issues:

**Why 11k emails were skipped:**
- The `daysSinceLastOrder` field is likely `null` or undefined for those users (maybe they've never ordered, or the field isn't populated)
- When `ifGte` gets a null value, Iterable can't evaluate the condition and skips the send entirely

**Why the links are broken:**
- `{{returnUrl}}` is probably `null` or empty for some users
- This creates malformed URLs like `?utm_source=iterable&utm_campaign=winback` (no domain)

Here's a fixed version with defensive checks:

```handlebars
{{#if daysSinceLastOrder}}
  {{#ifGte daysSinceLastOrder 90}}
    <p>It's been a while, {{firstName}}! Here's 20% off.</p>
    {{#if returnUrl}}
      <a href="{{returnUrl}}?utm_source=iterable&utm_campaign=winback">Shop now</a>
    {{else}}
      <a href="https://yoursite.com?utm_source=iterable&utm_campaign=winback">Shop now</a>
    {{/if}}
  {{else}}
    <p>Thanks for being a regular, {{firstName}}.</p>
  {{/ifGte}}
{{else}}
  <p>Welcome back! Here's 20% off your first order.</p>
  {{#if returnUrl}}
    <a href="{{returnUrl}}?utm_source=iterable&utm_campaign=winback">Shop now</a>
  {{else}}
    <a href="https://yoursite.com?utm_source=iterable&utm_campaign=winback">Shop now</a>
  {{/if}}
{{/if}}
```

To verify, check your Iterable user data:
1. Export a sample of the skipped users
2. Look for missing/null `daysSinceLastOrder` or `returnUrl` values

That'll confirm whether those fields are the problem.
